<title>CANADA: Alberta Wheat Pool forecasts above average crops.</title>
<headline>Alberta Wheat Pool forecasts above average crops.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberta Wheat Pool in its first weekly crop assessment of the 1997 growing season rated grain and oilseeds crops above average on June 16.</p>
<p>AWP's conditions index of 100 represents optimal growing conditions while 50 represents average crop output.</p>
<p>This week's index of 79 is above average and is above last year's assessment for the corresponding week at 76.</p>
<p>CROPS				CONDITIONS INDEX</p>
<p>				     1997	 1996</p>
<p>Hard Red Spring Wheat	  80	   77</p>
<p>Canada Prairie Spring Wheat  80	   78</p>
<p>Soft White Spring Wheat	61	   75</p>
<p>Winter Wheat		     62	   62</p>
<p>Durum Wheat			67	   68</p>
<p>Oats				 79	   78</p>
<p>Barley			     80	   75</p>
<p>Flax				 71	   72</p>
<p>Canola			     77	   73</p>
<p>Fall Rye			   68	   65</p>
<p>AVERAGE CROP CONDITION	 79	   76</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
